#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SoCLabs TideLink — SpyGlass CDC Constraints for axi_chiplet_controller
#
# This module is black-boxed (stop_module) in the top-level .prj file.
# These constraints declare the clock domain of each port so SpyGlass can
# verify CDC at the integration boundary.
#
# The chiplet controller receives apb_clk and app_clk (both = hclk) and
# user_hsclk (= user_ref_clk). Internal user_ref_clk <-> app_clk CDC is
# pre-verified by Wlink IP.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-08-17: this header used to read "All port-facing interfaces
# operate in the app_clk domain." That is NOT true and is a dangerous thing to
# leave written down here, because it is exactly the sentence that turns an
# unconstrained port into a wrong app_clk declaration. Fifteen ports on this
# boundary are in the link_rx_clk domain (the thirteen lane_*_o /
# lane_*_i signals below, plus obs_epoch_anchored_o / obs_epoch_span_o), and
# the PHY pads belong to the pad_clk_tx / pad_clk_rx domains. The bus and
# register interfaces are app_clk; nothing wider than that is safe to assume.
#
# THE RULE FOR THIS FILE: a WRONG clock declaration MASKS a real crossing; a
# MISSING one only over-reports. Establish a port's domain from the RTL before
# declaring it, and if you cannot, leave it in the "NOT YET CONSTRAINED" block
# at the end rather than pattern-matching a neighbour.
#
# Contributors
#
# David Mapstone (d.a.mapstone@soton.ac.uk)
#
# Copyright 2026, SoC Labs (www.soclabs.org)
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

current_design axi_chiplet_controller

# Clock: app_clk is connected to hclk at the top level
clock -name app_clk -domain hclk_domain -period 4.0

# 2026-08-17 — apb_clk was never declared, though the module has BOTH an
# app_clk and an apb_clk port and tidelink_top.sv ties them to the same net:
#     .apb_clk (hclk),
#     .app_clk (hclk),
# apb_clk is the clock most of the controller's SoC-Labs-added logic actually
# runs on — the observability CDC synchronisers (sync_obs_*), the autoneg
# instance (u_autoneg .clk(apb_clk)), the Wlink APB register file
# (gb2wl_clock = apb_clk), and the IRQ stickies all sit in it. Declaring it in
# the same domain as app_clk is a statement of fact from the instantiation,
# not an assumption, and it is what makes the app_clk declarations on the
# ports below internally consistent.
clock -name apb_clk -domain hclk_domain -period 4.0

# Recovered RX clock — divided-down (÷16) version of pad_clk_rx, generated
# inside the chiplet controller (deps/axi-chiplet-controller@3e0e711). It is
# exposed through link_rx_clk_o so the top-level tidelink_gpio_phy_apb_regs
# slave can use it as the destination domain for the new per-lane CDC paths.
# We name the local clock object after the output port so the alias resolves
# inside the blackboxed design unit.
clock -name link_rx_clk_o -domain link_rx_domain -period 64.0

# All output ports are in the app_clk (hclk) domain
abstract_port -ports "tidelink_out[*]"     -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "ptp_out[*]"          -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "tx_link_idle"        -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "axi_ini_0_*"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "axi_tgt_0_*"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_prdata[*]"       -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_pready"          -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_pslverr"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "generalbus_out[*]"   -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "s_i2c_axi_*"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "sb_reset_out"        -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "role_is_master_o"    -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "role_locked_o"       -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "ctrl_reg_rdata[*]"   -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "i2c_nbsy_irq"        -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "i2c_nrd_empty_irq"   -clock app_clk

# All input ports are in the app_clk (hclk) domain
abstract_port -ports "tidelink_in[*]"      -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "ptp_in[*]"           -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_psel"            -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_paddr[*]"        -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_penable"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_pprot[*]"        -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_pstrb[*]"        -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_pwrite"          -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_pwdata[*]"       -clock app_clk
# integ ACC override (src/rtl/local_overrides/axi_chiplet_controller.sv) renamed
# these three APB-side register-write inputs with an apb_ prefix; the SGDC port
# names must track the actual module ports or SpyGlass drops them as unmatched
# (SGDC_abstract_port02 Fatal -> Exit Code 7 -> the earlier "0 clocks / 0
# crossings" early-termination). The read-data OUTPUT stayed `ctrl_reg_rdata`
# (see abstract_port above).
abstract_port -ports "apb_ctrl_reg_write"  -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_ctrl_reg_addr[*]" -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_ctrl_reg_wdata[*]" -clock app_clk
# The same integ override added two APB read-region SELECT strobes to this same
# hclk-domain register interface: apb_ctrl_reg_r10 (perlane-wp Region-10 select)
# and apb_ctrl_reg_rd (rxcap Region-D select). Both are driven at top level by
# u_tidelink_fifo's ctrl_reg_r10 / ctrl_reg_rd outputs (that instance is clocked
# by .hclk(hclk)), i.e. they are hclk-domain siblings of the write/addr/wdata
# strobes above and covered by this SGDC's "all input ports are app_clk" model.
# They were omitted from the port enumeration, so SpyGlass could not bind their
# black-box-input domain and DEFAULTED them to user_ref_clk, manufacturing two
# spurious Ac_unsync01 hclk->user_ref_clk crossings (source domains: 1 = hclk).
# Declaring the true (app_clk=hclk) domain — the same constraint their siblings
# carry, NOT a waiver — collapses those to same-domain (non-crossing).
abstract_port -ports "apb_ctrl_reg_r10"    -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_ctrl_reg_rd"     -clock app_clk
# 2026-08-17 — IT RECURRED. `apb_ctrl_reg_rf` is the THIRD region-select strobe
# of the very interface whose first two (r10, rd) caused the incident described
# in the paragraph above, and it was omitted in exactly the same way. Verified
# present at src/rtl/local_overrides/axi_chiplet_controller.sv:254 ("AXI
# data-node observability 2026-07-29 (I4) — Region F disambiguator"), driven at
# top level by tidelink_top.sv:.apb_ctrl_reg_rf(ctrl_reg_rf) from
# u_tidelink_fifo, an hclk-clocked instance — i.e. the same domain as its two
# siblings, which is why the constraint is identical.
#
# WHY NO TOOL CAUGHT IT — and it is NOT the reason usually given. SpyGlass's
# unmatched-abstract_port detectors are SGDC_abstract_port02 ("'<port>' not
# found on/within module '<module>'") and SGDC_abstract_port21. Neither is
# waived anywhere in this tree, and both were live. They cannot catch this
# class of drift, because an OMITTED port produces no constraint for them to
# check — they only fire on a declaration that points at a name which no
# longer exists. The failure here is a declaration that was never written.
#
# (checkSGDC_05 is sometimes described as the unmatched-abstract_port
# detector. It is not — per the installed rule documentation it "checks if
# constraints are valid for non-top environments", i.e. it flags a constraint
# under a non-top current_design being auto-migrated to the top, which is what
# this very file does by design. Waiving it neither caused nor could have
# caught this.)
#
# So there is no rule to un-waive; a rule does not exist for this. The
# standing check is the static one — scripts/cdc/sgdc_port_drift.py, which
# compares declarations against the real port list in BOTH directions and
# needs no licence.
abstract_port -ports "apb_ctrl_reg_rf"     -clock app_clk
# Chiplet-controller hclk-domain inputs (§3.1 of prior sign-off)
abstract_port -ports "puf_ready"           -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "apb_debug_unlock_i"  -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "idelay_rst"          -clock app_clk

# v2 eye-visibility surface — driven by tidelink_eye_regs at top (hclk domain).
# Outputs from the controller calibrator are also exposed back to eye_regs in
# the app_clk domain (the calibrator FSM lives in app_clk inside the
# controller).
abstract_port -ports "swi_eye_lane_sel_i[*]"   -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "swi_eye_dwell_us_i[*]"   -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "swi_eye_ctrl_i[*]"       -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_score_idx_i[*]"      -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_status_o[*]"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_score_data_o[*]"     -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_score_lane_passed_o" -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_score_best_o[*]"     -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_score_best_slip_o[*]" -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_score_best_phase_o[*]" -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_last_slip_o[*]"      -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "eye_last_lane_fault_o[*]" -clock app_clk

# ── New ports introduced by tidelink-gpio-phy integration ──────────────────
# (deps/axi-chiplet-controller@68d625d ports + @3e0e711 link_rx_clk_o)
#
# All eleven lane_*_o output ports are driven from the link_rx_clk domain
# inside the controller (the new lane_checker lives entirely in link_rx_clk).
# The two control inputs (lane_lock_thresh_i, lane_clear_noise_i) are
# *consumed* inside the controller in the link_rx_clk domain (they come from
# u_gpio_phy_apb_regs.lock_thresh_o / clear_noise_pulse_o which are themselves
# the OUTPUTS of the 2-FF/3-FF synchronizer chains running on link_rx_clk).
# Declaring the port domain as link_rx_clk_o avoids a spurious crossing-into-
# app_clk error at the chiplet-controller boundary.
abstract_port -ports "lane_lock_thresh_i[*]"   -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_clear_noise_i"      -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_mismatch_pulse_o[*]" -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_wire_status_o[*]"   -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_dist_raw_o[*]"      -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_dist_voted_o[*]"    -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_dwell_min_dist_o[*]" -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_noise_min_o[*]"     -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_noise_max_o[*]"     -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_noise_mean_o[*]"    -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_noise_current_o[*]" -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_canary_pass_o[*]"   -clock link_rx_clk_o
abstract_port -ports "lane_canary_valid_o[*]"  -clock link_rx_clk_o

# link_rx_clk_o is itself the generated clock — already declared above via
# `clock -name link_rx_clk_o`. SpyGlass propagates the domain through the
# top-level net into the tidelink_gpio_phy_apb_regs.link_rx_clk pin.

# ── 2026-08-17 port reconciliation ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file was reconciled against the REAL module port list of the unit that
# actually compiles — src/rtl/local_overrides/axi_chiplet_controller.sv, 206
# ports — using scripts/cdc/sgdc_port_drift.py, which parses the RTL and needs
# no tool licence. Before this pass: 166 of 206 ports declared, 40 undeclared.
# Zero declarations were stale, so nothing here was pointing at a dead name;
# the drift was entirely one-directional (RTL grew, SGDC did not follow).
#
# After this pass: 179 of 206 declared, 27 undeclared, still zero stale.
#
# Of the 40, twelve are functional signals in a real clock domain that the
# black-box boundary needs told about and are declared below; apb_clk gains a
# `clock` object (above) rather than an abstract_port. The remaining 27 are
# clocks, resets, DFT, pads, straps, and three build-conditional ports that
# are deliberately NOT given an abstract_port — see the two blocks at the end
# of this file for each one and why.
#
# THE RULE APPLIED THROUGHOUT: a WRONG clock declaration MASKS a real crossing;
# a MISSING one only over-reports. So each port below carries the RTL evidence
# for its domain, and anything whose domain could not be established from the
# RTL was left undeclared rather than guessed.

# ── hclk-domain functional ports (app_clk) ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Observability outputs, all five driven from the far side of the existing
# 2-flop apb_clk synchronisers inside the controller (RTL lines 6394-6404,
# "drive the new module outputs from the apb_clk-synced 2-flop CDC
# registers"). apb_clk == app_clk == hclk at the tidelink_top instantiation,
# so these leave the black box already synchronised into the app domain. That
# is the whole point of those synchronisers; declaring them app_clk records
# it, and NOT declaring them was manufacturing crossings on signals whose
# synchroniser is right there in the source.
abstract_port -ports "obs_a2l_replay_link_valid_o" -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "obs_fe_rx_credit_max_o[*]"   -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "obs_fe_rx_is_full_o"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "obs_a2l_replay_app_valid_o"  -clock app_clk
# data_mode_o = sync_obs_fcsm_state_1[2] — bit 2 of the SAME apb_clk-synced
# FCSM state word. The RTL comment at line 504 states the domain explicitly
# ("Domain: apb_clk. Source is sync_obs_fcsm_state_1, the far side of the
# existing 2-flop apb_clk synchroniser").
abstract_port -ports "data_mode_o"                 -clock app_clk

# Interrupt / status outputs, all apb_clk flops or combinational functions of
# apb_clk flops:
#   train_fail_irq_o = train_fail_irq_r, set in the always_ff @(posedge
#       apb_clk or negedge poresetn) block at RTL line 2192.
#   nego_error_irq   = nego_error_irq_internal | nego_mask_mismatch_reg.
#       nego_error_irq_internal comes from u_autoneg, instantiated with
#       .clk(apb_clk); nego_mask_mismatch_reg is written in the always_ff
#       @(posedge apb_clk ...) block at RTL line 756.
#   interrupt        = u_wlink.interrupt, a pure OR of the Wlink APB register
#       file's W1C error stickies and their enables (Wlink.v:2097, sourced
#       from regs written in always @(posedge apb_clk ...) blocks).
abstract_port -ports "train_fail_irq_o"    -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "nego_error_irq"      -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "interrupt"           -clock app_clk

# generalbus_in — the input sibling of generalbus_out (already declared
# app_clk above). Consumed by Wlink's GeneralBusToWlink adapter, whose clock
# is assigned `gb2wl_clock = apb_clk` (Wlink.v:2449). tidelink_top currently
# ties this port to 32'h0, so the declaration is inert today; it is stated
# anyway so the constraint stays correct if a real driver is ever attached.
abstract_port -ports "generalbus_in[*]"    -clock app_clk

# Sideband reset / wake. Both are inert in this integration —
#   sb_reset_in  tied 1'b0            (tidelink_top.sv:2822)
#   sb_wake      output, unconnected  (tidelink_top.sv:2824)
# — so neither carries a crossing that a declaration could mask: a constant
# input has no domain to get wrong, and an output with no consumer has nothing
# downstream to mislead. They are declared app_clk anyway, matching the
# chiplet-level constraint for the same black box in
# cdc/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.sgdc:689-692, so the two files do not drift apart on
# the same module. Revisit if either is ever really driven.
abstract_port -ports "sb_reset_in"         -clock app_clk
abstract_port -ports "sb_wake"             -clock app_clk

# ── BUILD-CONDITIONAL PORTS — DELIBERATELY NOT DECLARED HERE ────────────────
#
# Three ports exist only when TIDELINK_PHY_V2 is defined
# (src/rtl/local_overrides/axi_chiplet_controller.sv:525-534, and the matching
# `ifdef at tidelink_top.sv:3106):
#
#     obs_epoch_anchored_o   link_rx_clk domain
#     obs_epoch_span_o[5:0]  link_rx_clk domain
#     xhb_sub_obs_word_i[31:0]  app_clk (hclk) domain
#
# Their domains ARE known — the RTL states them outright, at line 526
# ("link_rx_rx_link_clk domain; the APB slave 2-flop-syncs into apb_clk
# itself, so NO sync here") and again at line 4692 ("obs_epoch_anchored_o is
# the rx-link-clk-domain pass-through from Wlink"); xhb_sub_obs_word_i is the
# TL-009 leak witness driven from tidelink_top's XHB500 ahb_sub side
# (tidelink_top.sv:3112). Note especially that the first two are NOT app_clk:
# declaring them app_clk — the neighbouring default, and the obvious guess —
# would MASK a live link_rx_clk -> hclk crossing.
#
# They are nonetheless left UNDECLARED in this file, on purpose. SGDC has no
# preprocessor, and of the flists only tidelink_top_full_asic_v2 /
# tidelink_fpga / tidelink_fpga_v2 define TIDELINK_PHY_V2. The CDC Makefile's
# default is MODULE=tidelink_top -> flists/tidelink_top.flist, which does NOT.
# In that V1 build the three names match no port, and an unmatched
# abstract_port is SGDC_abstract_port02 FATAL -> exit code 7 -> a run that
# reports "0 clocks / 0 crossings" and looks like a tool fault. That exact
# failure is already on this file's record (see the note at the apb_ctrl_reg_*
# block above). Declaring them would trade a harmless over-report for a dead
# run.
#
# The chiplet-level SGDC (cdc/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.sgdc:767-785) DOES declare
# all three, correctly — its .prj defaults to an ASIC filelist that carries
# +define+TIDELINK_PHY_V2, so there the names always match. Both files are
# right for their own default build; that is why the constraint lives there
# and not here.
#
# IF THIS FILE IS EVER USED WITH A V2 FLIST (MODULE=tidelink_top_full_asic_v2,
# tidelink_fpga, tidelink_fpga_v2), add these three lines — and delete them
# again before going back to a V1 flist:
#
#   abstract_port -ports "obs_epoch_anchored_o"  -clock link_rx_clk_o
#   abstract_port -ports "obs_epoch_span_o[*]"   -clock link_rx_clk_o
#   abstract_port -ports "xhb_sub_obs_word_i[*]" -clock app_clk

# ── NOT YET CONSTRAINED — needs owner decision ──────────────────────────────
#
# 27 ports of axi_chiplet_controller have no abstract_port: the three
# build-conditional ones covered immediately above, plus the 24 grouped below.
# Every one is a deliberate omission, not an oversight; each is listed so the
# next reader does not have to re-derive the state of the file, and so the
# ones that are genuinely open are visible as open rather than absent.
#
# None of these may be given a domain by pattern-matching a neighbour. If one
# needs constraining, establish the domain from the RTL first — an over-report
# is recoverable, a wrong declaration is silent.
#
# (a) CLOCK PORTS — declared as clock objects, not abstract_ports:
#       app_clk, apb_clk        declared above (both tied to hclk)
#       link_rx_clk_o           declared above (generated, /16 of pad_clk_rx)
#       user_hsclk              Wlink PLL reference; declared at top scope in
#                               tidelink_top.sgdc as user_ref_clk
#       pad_clk_rx              declared at top scope in tidelink_top.sgdc
#       pad_clk_tx              TX-side launch clock, generated inside Wlink.
#                               OPEN: no clock object anywhere in this flow.
#       idelay_ref_clk          declared at top scope (FPGA-only 200 MHz ref)
#
# (b) RESET PORTS — declared at top scope in tidelink_top.sgdc via
#     `reset -name`, and covered by the targeted Ac_unsync01 waivers in
#     waiver.swl (synchronised by WavDemetReset inside Wlink):
#       poresetn, hresetn
#
# (c) DFT — held inactive by set_case_analysis at top scope; scan_out is a
#     scan-only output with no functional domain:
#       scan_mode, scan_asyncrst_ctrl, scan_clk, scan_shift, scan_in, scan_out
#
# (d) TRULY ASYNCHRONOUS EXTERNAL PADS — declaring any on-chip clock for these
#     would be a lie. The I2C lines are declared quasi_static at top scope and
#     are synchronised inside the controller; the D2D pads belong to the PHY
#     link domains, not to app_clk:
#       i2c_scl_i, i2c_scl_o, i2c_scl_t, i2c_sda_i, i2c_sda_o, i2c_sda_t
#       pad_rx      (declared pad_clk_rx domain at top scope)
#       pad_tx      OPEN: TX pad data, launched in the pad_clk_tx domain that
#                   has no clock object. Left undeclared on purpose — see (a).
#
# (e) STRAPS / QUASI-STATIC INPUTS — stable before reset deassertion, declared
#     quasi_static at top scope in tidelink_top.sgdc. They are not clocked by
#     anything, so an abstract_port on this boundary would assert something
#     false:
#       role_strap_i, mask_hs_bypass_i, nego_priority_i, puf_seed
#
# (f) CROSS-CHECK. Every domain asserted in this file was derived from the RTL
#     independently of cdc/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.sgdc, which constrains the same
#     black box at the chiplet level. Comparing the two afterwards: 69 ports
#     declared in both, ZERO domain disagreements — including the two that
#     matter most, obs_epoch_anchored_o / obs_epoch_span_o on link_rx_clk_o
#     rather than app_clk. Two independent derivations agreeing is not proof,
#     but it is the strongest evidence available without a tool run.
#
# Regenerate this reconciliation at any time with:
#     scripts/cdc/sgdc_port_drift.py --only axi_chiplet_controller
